\subsection{Research attempt}
\paragraph{Model, date and investigated scope.}
OpenAI GPT-6 Astra (configured model \texttt{gpt-6-astra}), ultra reasoning; generated 11 October 2026. Exhibits infinitely many rank-two based rings, showing that a coefficient-bound argument needs genuine categorification constraints.

\paragraph{Sources and literature check.}
The complete supplied definition, including source qualifications and the dated literature assessment, was reviewed. The calculation below is an elementary restricted attempt motivated by [S2]; it does not claim novelty or a fresh literature-status determination.

\paragraph{Context and investigated scope.} The complete supplied definition, including source qualifications and the dated literature assessment, was reviewed. The calculation below is an elementary restricted attempt motivated by [S2]; it does not claim novelty or a fresh literature-status determination.

\paragraph{Testing whether rank bounds the fusion coefficients.} For every integer $n\geq0$, consider the free abelian group with basis $1,x$ and multiplication
\[
 1x=x1=x,\qquad x^2=1+nx,\qquad x^*=x.
\]
It is an associative based ring: it is the quotient $\mathbb Z[t]/(t^2-nt-1)$ with the displayed basis, all structure constants are nonnegative, and the coefficient of $1$ in $xx^*$ is one. Its positive dimension assignment sends
\[
 x\longmapsto d_n=\frac{n+\sqrt{n^2+4}}2,
\]
since $d_n^2=1+nd_n$. Thus even rank two allows unbounded candidate fusion coefficients at the level of these elementary ring axioms.

\paragraph{Why categorification is the essential missing input.} A fusion category would additionally need associativity isomorphisms satisfying pentagon equations, duality data and, for the ribbon question, braiding and twist constraints. The constructed rings are not asserted to admit any of those structures. For $n=0$ the ring is the group ring of the two-element group, but this endpoint does not authorize the same conclusion for arbitrary $n$.

\paragraph{Attempt outcome.} The naive enumeration route ``fixed rank gives finitely many nonnegative multiplication tables'' is false before categorical constraints are used: the tables above already form an infinite sequence. Therefore a proof of the source conjecture must bound categorifiable coefficients using substantially more than positivity, rigidity-style coefficient identities and the rank. Neither a bound on actual categories nor finiteness of compatible ribbon structures is established. This is consistent with the source's separate known low-rank results and does not challenge their classification.

\paragraph{Verification and adversarial audit.}
Checked quotient associativity, nonnegative coefficients, duality coefficient and positive root; avoided claiming the rings are fusion categories. Model self-audit only; no independent human proof checking. Prompts A and B were applied to this canonical record and its qualified source scope. Checked quotient associativity, nonnegative coefficients, duality coefficient and positive root; avoided claiming the rings are fusion categories. Retained unresolved status and zero original-target progress; No bound on categorifiable fusion coefficients or count of actual fusion/ribbon structures is obtained.

Coordinator checked the rank-two based-ring multiplication and positive dimension equation. No categorification is assumed. This additional check was model-assisted, not independent human verification.

\paragraph{Tools, process and contributions.}
Python 3 was used for file preparation and structural checks; no numerical experiment or theorem prover was used. Contribution prompt A was followed by prompt B. GPT-6 Astra with ultra reasoning drafted the research and performed its stated self-audit; any additional coordinator contribution is identified in the verification and audit. A GPT-6-based Codex coordinator assembled the manuscript and checked repository integration; its exact variant and reasoning configuration were not exposed. No human mathematical contribution, independent human proof check or formal proof certification is supplied. Complete derivations and the consulted source references are included here; private reasoning transcripts are not published.

\paragraph{Final status and first remaining gap.}
\textbf{UNRESOLVED}. No bound on categorifiable fusion coefficients or count of actual fusion/ribbon structures is obtained.

